## 2. x402: HTTP Payments for AI Agents

`x402` is one of the more interesting pieces of the Stellar AI tooling landscape.

It turns the HTTP `402 Payment Required` response into a real payment flow that AI agents can handle.

### How it works
- A client hits a paywalled endpoint
- The server returns a `402` response with payment instructions
- The client signs a Soroban auth entry
- The client retries the request with the required payment data

### Why it matters
This is useful for products where AI agents need to:
- pay for API calls
- pay for gated services
- trigger small programmable financial actions
- operate autonomously with Stellar-native payment logic

### Useful links
- Docs: https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/apps/x402
- Monorepo: https://github.com/stellar/x402-stellar
- Example demo: https://github.com/jamesbachini/x402-Stellar-Demo

For most StellarX teams, this is not a default requirement. But if your project includes agents, paid APIs, or programmable service access, it is worth understanding.

